  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LC020 now flags a StringComparison overload whose query column flows through a method argument, not only its receiver. The constant-receiver, column-argument form (for example \"admin\".Contains(u.Name, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) inside a Where) was previously missed even though EF Core cannot translate the overload and throws at runtime on the default relational providers. Detection now considers the receiver and every argument for query-parameter dependence; constant and captured-local arguments stay quiet, and the existing fixer drops the StringComparison argument.",
